# Commits and comments

## Commits

- Use Conventional Commits: `type(scope): subject`.
- Scopes: `api` | `bot` | `web` | `core` | `qq` | `card` | `docs` | `repo` | `rules`.
- Subject: imperative; Chinese or English OK; one language per commit; explain why in body when non-obvious.
- No vague subjects (`update`, `WIP`, `fix stuff`).
- Full rules: `docs/COMMIT_CONVENTION.md`.

## Comments

- Prefer clarity via names/types; comment only **why**, invariants, workarounds, or non-obvious constraints.
- **No noise**: no narrating `i++`, no commented-out dead code, no obvious restatements.
- **Public exports** (`packages/core`, public API helpers): TSDoc/JSDoc in **English**.
- **Inline comments**: Chinese or English; prefer one language per file.
- TODOs: `TODO(scope): …` or `TODO: …` with actionable text; optional ticket/owner. No bare `TODO`.
- Full rules: `docs/CODING_STANDARDS.md` §注释.
